  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency capacity strengthening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SNPS-CC has more than 60 years of experience in implementing humanitarian emergency response programmes financed by international cooperation and the Colombian government, through the Ecclesiastical Jurisdictions, which are its partners on the ground with the capacity to attend places that, due to their distance or because they are located in areas of ongoing armed conflict, other agencies cannot attend. In addition, the Catholic Church is recognised in Colombia as one of the first responders in humanitarian crises caused by natural and anthropogenic events and derived from the armed conflict through a warm and comprehensive response to the main needs of affected families and individuals. 
Colombia is a country with permanent crises and diverse causes. However, in recent years, there has been an increase in crises that have more than one cause, making their response more complex. 
This project seeks to improve emergency response capacity of SNPS/CC and Ecclesiastical Jurisdictions, especially towards enabling a timelier response.</narrative>
  </description>
